  "note": "Borough elections, 15 January 1931, held under the revised system of an annual quota. Four members were returned for each ward from a single poll, one of whom the council afterwards recognised as the ward's alderman. Dr. Bowman was the ward's alderman; the councillors in order of priority were Davidson, M'Cleery and Miller."
